# Target C: double touch-three union-kernel deficiency drop

Date: 2026-09-23

Status: rigorous strengthening of the sole remaining eight-no-root `k=6,D=-1,p=9` Profile B. The preceding forcing theorem proves that every genuine source has at least two distinct dependency-active aligned touch-three singleton blocks. This note derives a new constraint from the interaction of the two forced puncture kernels.

Profile B and Target C-II are not yet closed.

Companion exact filter:

`research/verify_target_c_support7_global_segment_relative_eight_noroot_k6_dminus1_profile_b_double_touch3_union_kernel_2026_09_23.py`

## 1. Setup

Use the fixed source-basis model already proved in the kernel-lattice reduction:

```text
V = Q^9,
q_1,...,q_9 is the chosen source singleton basis,
L = W^perp <= V,
dim L = 6.
```

Let `b=q_i` and `c=q_j` be two distinct dependency-active aligned touch-three witnesses. Write `T,U` for their three source-coordinate touch sets. The previous geometry gives

```text
|T intersect U| <= 1.
```

For each witness, the distinguished puncture-kernel theorem gives

```text
K_T = E_T direct-sum <q_i>,
K_U = E_U direct-sum <q_j>,
```

where `E_T,E_U <= L` are the three-dimensional external kernel spans generated by the corresponding one-coordinate puncture lines.

Put

```text
R = T union U,
r = |R| in {5,6},
t = 8-r in {3,2}.
```

The theorem below applies whenever deleting all coordinates in `R` preserves coefficient rank two.

## 2. Double-witness union-kernel theorem

Assume the projected coefficient plane after deleting `R` still has rank two. Then the coordinate functionals indexed by `R` are independent on the six-dimensional coefficient nullspace. Hence

```text
E_R := span{ell_s : s in R}
```

has dimension `r`, and

```text
E_T + E_U = E_R.                                  (2.1)
```

Let

```text
K_R = ker(V -> V_R)
```

be the source-basis kernel of the `t`-row descendant. Puncture functoriality gives

```text
K_T <= K_R,
K_U <= K_R.
```

Therefore

```text
span(E_R,q_i,q_j) <= K_R.                          (2.2)
```

Define the exact internal increment

```text
sigma_R = dim span(E_R,q_i,q_j) - dim E_R.
```

Both witnesses are dependency-active, so neither `q_i` nor `q_j` belongs to `L`, while `E_R <= L`. Thus

```text
sigma_R in {1,2}.                                  (2.3)
```

Let `d_R` be the virtual-canonical complete deficiency of the rank-two `t`-row descendant. The nine source basis classes map surjectively onto its replacement-functional quotient. For a rank-two coefficient plane that quotient has dimension

```text
dim V_R = (t-2) + d_R.
```

Consequently

```text
dim K_R = 9 - ((t-2)+d_R)
        = 11 - t - d_R.                            (2.4)
```

From (2.2), `dim E_R = r = 8-t`, and the definition of `sigma_R`,

```text
dim K_R >= (8-t) + sigma_R.                        (2.5)
```

Combining (2.4) and (2.5) gives

```text
d_R <= 3 - sigma_R.                                (2.6)
```

Since `sigma_R>=1`, every rank-preserving union puncture of two forced touch-three witnesses satisfies

```text
d_R <= 2.                                          (2.7)
```

Thus the union puncture can never remain in deficiency three.

If `sigma_R=2`, then

```text
d_R <= 1.                                          (2.8)
```

In particular, if the two witness source coordinates are linearly independent modulo `L`, then `sigma_R=2`, so (2.8) holds.

## 3. Rigidity of the borderline d_R=2 case

Suppose the union puncture preserves coefficient rank two and has `d_R=2`. Then (2.6) forces

```text
sigma_R=1.
```

Equivalently, the two internal witness directions collapse to one dimension modulo `E_R`:

```text
q_i - lambda q_j in E_R
```

for some nonzero rational `lambda` after rescaling one witness coordinate. Since `E_R <= L`, the two witness classes are also projectively equal in `V/L`.

Therefore a rank-preserving double-witness union with deficiency two is highly nongeneric: it requires an exact source-basis relation supported by the external union-kernel space. Any pair with independent images in `V/L`, or more generally with `sigma_R=2`, forces deficiency at most one.

## 4. Exact source-level filter

The companion verifier is layered on the existing exact kernel-lattice and touch-three-witness audit. For every fixed nine-block source basis it:

1. reconstructs all distinguished active aligned touch-three witnesses exactly;
2. requires at least two, using the preceding forcing theorem;
3. checks every witness pair has distinct touch triples with intersection at most one;
4. forms `R=T union U`;
5. if deleting `R` drops coefficient rank, records that rank-drop branch but does not reject it using this theorem;
6. if coefficient rank remains two, reconstructs the exact descendant canonical state and source-basis kernel;
7. checks puncture functoriality `K_T,K_U <= K_R` directly;
8. computes `E_R` and `sigma_R` exactly over `Fraction`;
9. rejects any state with

```text
d_R > 3-sigma_R.
```

The code also checks the equivalent dimension inequality

```text
dim K_R >= dim span(E_R,q_i,q_j).
```

This is a necessary filter. A full zero-survivor cover would close Profile B; a survivor remains a candidate.

## 5. Remaining bottleneck

Every remaining Profile B source now has at least two distinguished touch-three witnesses. For each pair, either:

- the union puncture drops coefficient rank, creating a low-support coefficient-codeword branch on five or six deleted coordinates; or
- the union puncture preserves coefficient rank and its descendant deficiency is at most two, with deficiency two possible only under the exact collapse `sigma_R=1`.

The next target is to run this double-witness filter on the fixed-nine cover, then attack the rank-drop union branch and any `sigma_R=1,d_R=2` survivors separately.
